# Reporting Deadlines for Aid Distribution

This scope calculates the required deadlines for reporting aid distribution activities based on the date of arrival and the date of delivery completion.

```catala
declaration scope ArticleVIIIReporting:
  input arrival_date content date
  input delivery_completion_date content date
  input reference_date content date
  output report_30_days_due content date
  output report_1_month_due content date
  output is_30_days_late content boolean
  output is_1_month_late content boolean
```

## 30-Day Reporting Deadline

The first report must be submitted no later than 30 days after the arrival of each shipment at the place of delivery.

```catala
scope ArticleVIIIReporting:
  date round down
  definition report_30_days_due equals
    arrival_date + 30 day
```

## One-Month Reporting Deadline

The second report must be submitted one month after the completion of the delivery.

```catala
scope ArticleVIIIReporting:
  definition report_1_month_due equals
    delivery_completion_date + 1 month
```

## Checking Reporting Lateness

This scope checks whether the reference date indicates that either the 30-day or the one-month reporting deadline has passed.

```catala
scope ArticleVIIIReporting:
  definition is_30_days_late equals
    reference_date > report_30_days_due
  definition is_1_month_late equals
    reference_date > report_1_month_due
```